  "title": "Schur (2,2) reconstruction for explicit length classes",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "Let n>=2 and c_j(n)=n*(n^2-1+3*2^(j-1)-3^j)/3. If c_j(n) is nonzero for every 1<=j<=n, then every n-element multiset of positive real numbers, including repetitions, is uniquely determined by the cardinality and first n logarithmic power sums of its complete Schur-(2,2) monomial-value multiset, with tableau multiplicities. This condition holds for every n>=3 with n!=4 and n modulo 60 outside {14,26,34,46}. Moreover, lengths 2 and 4 are uniquely reconstructible when the positive input sum is prescribed. Consequently, for every integer N>=2, positive integer partitions lambda,mu of N of length at least two and common length outside {14,26,34,46} modulo 60 satisfy S22(lambda)=S22(mu) only if lambda=mu. Equal output cardinalities force equal lengths. No converse, counterexample at an excluded length, or all-length resolution is claimed. Exact scope and proofs are Theorems A--C of evidence/research-moment-proof.md.",
